# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/compression-header.md#algorithm-byte
# provenance: PV-0060, PV-0061, PV-0062, PV-0063, PV-0065, PV-0066, PV-0067, PV-0069, PV-0080, PV-0310, PV-0311, PV-0312
# kind: compression-header
# description: LZC header: algorithm byte 0x11 is LZC (the dissectors' 0x10 label is wrong); byte 7 = maxbits 16 with the block-mode bit 0x80.
# derivation: 256 as u32 LE = 00 01 00 00 (PV-0061, PV-0062); 0x11 = version 1, algorithm 1 = LZC (PV-0063, PV-0065); magic (PV-0067); byte 7 = 0x90: maxbits = 0x90 & 0x1F = 16 (PV-0069, PV-0310, reading R-CH-5 as corrected in v1; 16 within PV-0080, PV-0311), block mode 1 (PV-0312), unused bits 0x00.
# expect.error: none
# expect.uncompressed_length: 256
# expect.algorithm: lzc
# expect.version: 1
# expect.maxbits: 16
# expect.block_mode: 1
# expect.unused_bits: 0x00
hex:
00 01 00 00                                       # uncompressed length, u32 LE
11                                                # algorithm byte
1F 9D                                             # magic
90                                                # byte 7
